[B][SIZE=6]CustomDeathMessages 2.1.0[/SIZE][/B]

[B][SIZE=5]Highlights[/SIZE][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Fixed death messages breaking on 1.8 - 1.12.0 whenever a head dropped.
[*]Fixed PvP deaths showing no death message at all on 26.x.
[*]Item hovers now show the weapon's real name, enchantments and lore on every version (1.16+ showed a plain item).
[*]Deaths are credited correctly: no more "You killed ..." for a player who only hit someone before they fell, no stale killers after cancelled hits or totems, and dying to your own arrow is not a PvP kill.
[*]Hover messages now respect the [ICODE]showDeathMessages[/ICODE] gamerule, vanish plugins and cancelled deaths, and Discord bridges forward them with their own formatting.
[*]A typo in [ICODE]config.yml[/ICODE] can no longer wipe your messages: [ICODE]/cdm reload[/ICODE] keeps the working config and shows the line of the error.
[*]New mobs: add a list named after any mob or damage cause (for example [ICODE]creaking-messages[/ICODE]) and it is used automatically.
[*]Item names and nicknames can no longer inject colors or placeholders into death messages.
[*][ICODE]/deathmessage[/ICODE] works again.
[/LIST]

[B][SIZE=5]Changes[/SIZE][/B]
[LIST]
[*]An empty message list now uses the vanilla death message; a blank message ([ICODE]""[/ICODE]) hides it. The last message of a list can be removed.
[*][ICODE]/cdm list[/ICODE] shows the raw text with [ICODE]&[/ICODE] codes, [ICODE]/cdm set number[/ICODE] validates values.
[*][ICODE]message-cooldown[/ICODE] now only limits the global death message.
[*]Heads are added to the death drops so grave plugins can pick them up.
[*]Hex colors are approximated on servers older than 1.16.
[*]Update checks no longer contact SpigotMC on every login.
[*]New installs have lightning and head drops turned off by default (existing configs are unchanged).
[/LIST]

[B][SIZE=5]Notes[/SIZE][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Supports Spigot and Paper 1.8 through 26.x.
[*]Your config is updated automatically ([ICODE]config-version[/ICODE] 4); your messages and settings are kept.
[*]If you use head drops: they never actually worked before 2.0.2, so check [ICODE]drop-head-percentage[/ICODE] (the old default was 0.5 = 50%).
[*]Plugins listening to [ICODE]CustomPlayerDeathEvent[/ICODE] should use [ICODE]PlayerDeathEvent[/ICODE] instead.
[/LIST]
